{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "793e7fba-e0e6-8712-8325-dbb42c805fc3",
  "created_at": "2026-01-21T12:53:30-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Yesenia Salazar",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:49:38-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:49:42-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good afternoon, Mr. Ferreira. My name is Yesenia Salazar. I would like to inquire about my water and sewer bill, because I received it yesterday and I do not understand one of the lines."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:49:53-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, happy to walk through it. What's the line that's tripping you up?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:49:58-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It says the reading type is, um, E-S-T. And the amount is much higher than usual. I believe that nobody ever came to read my meter. I have not seen anyone at my house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:50:09-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so EST means estimated. When the meter doesn't get read, we bill based on your past usage, kind of an educated guess. It doesn't always mean someone skipped you. Sometimes the reader can't get to the meter, or the remote signal didn't come through."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:50:23-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. But then how can it be so high, if it is based on what I used before? I would like to understand that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:50:31-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. If your earlier usage was higher, say a bigger bill in the summer, the estimate can lean on that. Then when we get an actual read, it corrects up or down."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:50:41-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So the next bill will fix it? Or do I owe this amount now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:50:46-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The next actual read adjusts it. You'd see a credit if the estimate was too high. But if you think the number's off, we can send someone to read it for real."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:50:56-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] Excuse me one moment. I am at my work, and there are clippers going behind me. I cut hair at a barbershop on the avenue. Can you hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:51:05-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you fine, a little buzzing, that's all. No worries."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:51:09-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Now, I should also say that I had a plumber at the house recently. I kept the receipt. Is that important for this?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:51:17-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It could be. If he did repairs, a leak or a running toilet, that would change your usage. Hang onto the receipt. What did he work on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:51:26-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "He replaced a part in the toilet, I believe it is called a flapper. Is that what you would call a leak?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:51:33-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, that's a classic one. A bad flapper can run water all day. So if the real read shows high use before the repair, the receipt helps explain it. I'll put in a request for an actual meter read."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:51:45-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That would be very kind. Do I need to give you the account number? I have it written here, but I am not certain which number it is. There is one at the top and one at the bottom."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:51:57-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The one at the top right is the account number. The bottom is the payment stub reference. Go ahead and read the top one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:52:05-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[line breaks up] It is... [inaudible] ...I am sorry, is the bottom one the one with the dashes?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:52:11-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, the one with the dashes is the account number. Take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:52:16-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, I understand now. Thank you. I will come back to that. First, I would like to ask something else. If I decide to pay before the reading, is there a way to pay outside regular hours? I cannot leave the shop during the day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:52:30-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there's a drop box at City Hall for payments, so you can drop a check in after we close. Just put your account number on the check and use the stub."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:52:40-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A drop box. And it is available at night, also on the weekend?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:52:45-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, it's outside, so you can use it any time. We pick up what's in there on business days."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:52:51-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Very good. But if it is only an estimate, should I pay all of it or wait for the correct reading?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:52:58-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Honestly, I'd get the read scheduled first, and call us back after. If you wait a few days on it, we can tell you the right amount to send."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:53:07-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. So I wait, and then I pay the correct amount. I think I understand, although I am still a little unsure about the credit part."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:53:16-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Totally fair. Short version: estimate too high, the next real read takes it back off your bill. I'll note your call today."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:53:23-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you very much, Mr. Ferreira. You have been patient with me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T12:53:27-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Anytime, Ms. Salazar. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
